🎯 RECOMMENDED: Pehle Structure, Fir Code
Bhai, ek smart approach bata raha hun — interviewers ko ye bahut pasand aata hai:

Approach: Incremental Commits
Ek saath sab kuch upload mat karo. Step-by-step upload karo — isse tumhara contribution graph bhi accha dikhta hai aur history bhi clean rehti hai.

Commit sequence:

bash
# 1. Project skeleton
git add README.md .gitignore
git commit -m "docs: add README and gitignore"
git push

# 2. Backend structure
git add backend/
git commit -m "feat: add FastAPI backend structure with models, routers, services"
git push

# 3. Digital Twin engine
git add backend/app/digital_twin/
git commit -m "feat: implement digital twin simulation engine"
git push

# 4. RL agent
git add backend/app/rl_agent/
git commit -m "feat: add PPO reinforcement learning agent with Gym environment"
git push

# 5. Gemini integration
git add backend/app/llm/
git commit -m "feat: integrate Google Gemini for insight generation"
git push

# 6. Database
git add database/
git commit -m "feat: add SQL schema and migrations"
git push

# 7. Frontend
git add frontend/
git commit -m "feat: add React dashboard with TailwindCSS and Recharts"
git push
💡 Bonus: Interview me bol sakte ho — "Sir, maine incremental commits use kiye taaki project history clean rahe." → 10/10 impression ✅

🐛 Common Errors & Fixes
Error	Fix
remote origin already exists	git remote remove origin fir dobara add karo
failed to push some refs	git pull origin main --rebase fir git push
Authentication failed	Personal Access Token use karo (password nahi)
node_modules upload ho gaya	.gitignore banao, fir git rm -r --cached node_modules
file too large (100MB+)	Git LFS use karo ya file remove karo
fatal: not a git repository	git init chalao pehle
